lready bricked by the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]defect; the bead event log can no longer be persisted ahead of the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]state it derives; the dead wake-due-snooze selector is gone from [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the Rust core; the two rival snooze parsers are one; `sase bead [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]list` shows snoozed beads by default like `sase bead search` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]already does; and epic sase-gn is closed with its plan file marked [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]done.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]snooze_close_corruption.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/snooze_close_corruption.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]202608/bead_snooze_and_notification_indicator.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-gn.10[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-gn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-gn.10.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop a close from bricking a snoozed bead's store[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]snooze-close-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snooze-close-core: clear the snooze record on every transition out of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]snoozed in both the mutation and the reducer, validate derived issues [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]before the event log is written, and delete the orphaned wake-due-snooze[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]selector.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Non-mocked close regression coverage and the core pin bump[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]snooze-close-regression[dim] · [dim][/dim]after snooze-close-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snooze-close-regression: pin the sase-core release carrying the fix and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cover both close call sites against a real bead store, closing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mocking gap that let the corruption ship.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One snooze wake-time parser, not two[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]snooze-parser-merge[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snooze-parser-merge: collapse snooze_time.py and snooze_duration.py into[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a single parser so the CLI and the gate/ACE surfaces cannot accept [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]different wake-time forms.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Snoozed beads stay visible in the default listing[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]snooze-list-default[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snooze-list-default: add snoozed to `sase bead list`'s default status [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]set and correct the help text and docs that still enumerate the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pre-snooze status list.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Close epic sase-gn[/bold #D7AFFF]                                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]snooze-gn-land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after snooze-close-core, snooze-close-regression, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]snooze-parser-merge, snooze-list-default[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snooze-gn-land: close epic sase-gn with a close note covering the whole [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]landing, run symvision, and mark the sase-gn plan file done.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-gn.10